P2: A running warrant serve does not see newly fetched merge receipts until a local store/config file changes or the reader restarts. D requires readers to see each merge through the receipts source. The declaration and key binding are present, but this reader's source-reading behavior is incomplete.

Cause: warrant_agent/serve.py:247-257. Space._stamp reads only the local .warrant/*.json and *.jsonl files' sizes and mtimes. Space.report returns the cached report before Repo.report can read changed source refs (warrant/repo.py:61-64 and warrant/sources.py:108-121). Fetching refs/heads/receipts, including its ordinary refs/remotes/origin/receipts form, changes Git data alone, so a warmed server keeps the previous union indefinitely. This is local cache staleness even after the clone has obtained the receipts, not a claim that a reader must fetch the network itself. A source becoming available for the first time is the same missing cache dependency.

Independent reproduction using actual gate receipts: with the checkout fixed at M, load Space at receipts tip 99606d1225b6e6edb44725c819c82ed2dfd19905 (98 receipts), then advance only its remote-tracking receipts ref to cbc96c14b1c7acab97ac3a7bac32f539537618fb (105). The warmed report stays the identical object and snapshot with 98 merge-gate records. A fresh Space and source read see 105; all 105 have basis SIGNED under M's trust. These Git-ref changes were made only in a disposable review copy.

The self-contained fixture below uses deterministic test keys, two correctly formed signed receipts produced by warrant.receipt.file, and fresh temporary Git repositories. It requires no network or operator seeds. From a checkout of M, save it outside that checkout and run python3 /path/to/receipt_cache_probe.py with TMPDIR inside the review work directory. Expected: after the fetch, the warmed reader sees both signed observations as a fresh reader does. Observed: first=1, warmed=1, fresh=2; exit 1 with the named FAIL.

```python
"""Run from the checkout of M: python3 /path/to/receipt_cache_probe.py."""
import json
import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path[:0] = [str(Path.cwd()), str(Path.cwd() / "tests")]
from world import Repo, KEYS, git
from warrant import receipt as RC
from warrant_agent.serve import Space

r = Repo(git_init=True)
target = r.entity("alice", "obligation@1", {"state": "open", "statement": "merge target", "serves": []})
key = KEYS["eve"]  # deterministic fixture key, never an operator's key
r.trust["keys"]["merge-gate"] = [key.public]
r.write_config()
(r.dot / "sources.json").write_text(json.dumps({"warrant": "sources/1", "sources": [
    {"name": "receipts", "ref": "refs/heads/receipts", "actors": ["merge-gate"]}]}))
source = r.home / "receipts"

def add_receipt(n):
    merge, tip, base = f"{n:040x}", "a" * 40, "b" * 40
    gate = {"pr": n, "merged": True, "merge": merge, "head": tip, "base": base, "version": target}
    pull = {"number": n, "merged": True, "merge_commit_sha": merge, "head": {"sha": tip}}
    commit = {"sha": merge, "parents": [{"sha": base}, {"sha": tip}], "commit": {
        "message": f"merge-on-acceptance: solo: head version {target} by claude at {tip}, one model family"}}
    RC.file(source, gate, pull, commit, "acme/widget", key, at=1_900_000_000 + n)
    if n == 1:
        git(source, "init", "-q", "-b", "receipts")
    git(source, "add", ".warrant")
    git(source, "commit", "-q", "-m", f"fixture receipt {n}")
    git(r.root, "fetch", "-q", str(source), "+refs/heads/receipts:refs/remotes/origin/receipts")

def count(rep):
    return sum(x["actor"] == "merge-gate" for x in rep["_recs"].values())

add_receipt(1)
space = Space({"warrant": str(r.root)})
first = space.report("warrant")
stamp = space._stamp(r.root)
add_receipt(2)
warm = space.report("warrant")
fresh = Space({"warrant": str(r.root)}).report("warrant")
result = {"first": count(first), "warmed": count(warm), "fresh": count(fresh),
          "local_stamp_unchanged": stamp == space._stamp(r.root),
          "same_cached_object": first is warm,
          "fresh_snapshot_differs": fresh["snapshot"] != warm["snapshot"],
          "all_fresh_receipts_signed": all(fresh["_basis"][i] == "SIGNED" for i, x in fresh["_recs"].items()
                                           if x["actor"] == "merge-gate")}
print(json.dumps(result, indent=1))
assert result["first"] == 1 and result["fresh"] == 2 and result["all_fresh_receipts_signed"]
if count(warm) != count(fresh):
    print("FAIL RECEIPT_SOURCE_REFRESH warmed warrant serve hides the newly fetched signed merge receipt")
    sys.exit(1)
print("ok   RECEIPT_SOURCE_REFRESH warmed reader refreshed the receipts source")
```

